// Brought to u by MidManStudio
//
// Docs only, 3 anchored edits. (1) and (2) docs/LLVM_ROADMAP.md: the "Where things stand" table stops at slice 4;
// it now points to docs/LLVM_BACKEND_STATUS.md and keeps the old table as history. (3) web/site/src/project-status.md:
// the Phase 4 row still describes the first slice ("int and bool functions, control flow, arena blocks"); this is
// a public page, so op 3 is yours to keep, reword or delete. Delete it (the last line of the DATA block) and the
// "patched : N" line must say 2 instead of 3.
//
// Needs docs/LLVM_BACKEND_STATUS.md on master (the ubel-llvm-arena-4 tarball). Checked against master 044017b:
// every anchor matches exactly once. Run it with dry_run on first.

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0",
  author     -> "MidManStudio",
  features   -> "quickfuncs,data",
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@QUICKFUNCS(
  ~patch_replace_text<object>(_path, _anchor, _content) {
    return { path = _path, op = "replace_text", anchor = _anchor, content = _content }
  }
)

@DATA(
  patch_files::
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_ROADMAP.md", "## Where things stand\n\n| Slice | What it adds | Evidence |", "## Where things stand\n\n**See `docs/LLVM_BACKEND_STATUS.md`, which is kept current**: what exists, what the backend does not compile yet\n(measured), how far it is from a real executable, and the milestones. In short, as of 2026-11-09: slices 1 to 4\nand A5 to A9 are done (strings, closures, enums and `match`, Unicode string methods, the target program\n`ast_builder.ubl`); the next blockers are collections, the numeric tower, generics and a `ubel build` command.\n\nSlices 1 to 4, as first written (kept as history):\n\n| Slice | What it adds | Evidence |")
    patch_replace_text("docs/LLVM_ROADMAP.md", "The target program's first refusal is now its `string` payload (`Var(string)`), so the next\nblocker is strings, and behind strings closures.", "(The sentence that followed this table when it was written, \"the next blocker is strings, and behind strings\nclosures\", is out of date: both landed and the target program compiles.)")
    patch_replace_text("web/site/src/project-status.md", "| 4 | Started | LLVM backend, native binaries. So far a proof of concept: hand-written IR measures the three tiers, and a small emitter turns a subset of Ubel (int and bool functions, control flow, arena blocks) into LLVM IR that matches the interpreter (`docs/LLVM_POC.md`) |", "| 4 | Started | LLVM backend, native binaries. Hand-written IR measured the three tiers, and an emitter turns a growing subset of Ubel into LLVM IR that is checked against the interpreter at every step: int, bool and string values, structs, enums and `match`, closures, arenas and the garbage-collected heap, Unicode string methods. The target program `examples/arena_demo/ast_builder.ubl` compiles. Collections, floats and sized integers, generics, traits and a `ubel build` command are not there yet (`docs/LLVM_BACKEND_STATUS.md`) |")
)
